namespace pdg { /**
\fn object pdg::NetServer::ready()
\brief Wait until the requested listeners are bound.

Returns a Promise resolving to an array of bound listener addresses, including
transport, address, port and secure. WebSocket entries also contain path.
server.listeners.native and server.listeners.websocket contain these snapshots,
or null when unavailable. Call listen() first. With the default atomic startup,
a failed listener closes all requested listeners and rejects the Promise. With
allowPartialListen, individual failures reach onError() and successfully bound
addresses resolve; failure of every listener still rejects.

\return Promise of the bound address array.
\see listen(), shutdown(), \ref websocket_server_options
**/ }

namespace pdg { /**
\var string pdg::NetConnection::transport
\brief Read-only carrier name: native or websocket.

onMessage() continues to report "tcp" for reliable messages and "udp" for
native datagrams. Inspect transport to identify the carrier. WebSocket reports
hasDgram as false, so sendDgram() uses send().
**/ }

namespace pdg { /**
\var boolean pdg::NetConnection::secure
\brief Read-only indication that the carrier uses TLS.

True for wss://, false for ws:// and native TCP. Browser localAddr and remoteAddr
are empty strings; localPort and remotePort are zero because browser APIs do not
expose socket endpoints. Native runtimes populate the available endpoints.
**/ }

namespace pdg { /**
\var boolean pdg::hasNetworkClient
\brief True when NetClient is available.

Browser WebSocket, iOS JavaScriptCore TCP/UDP and WebSocket, and standalone runtimes expose clients. hasNetwork remains
the broad networking capability flag; use hasNetworkServer before hosting.
**/ }

namespace pdg { /**
\var boolean pdg::hasNetworkServer
\brief True when NetServer and incoming listeners are available.

True in standalone and Node runtimes, false in browser and iOS/JSC runtimes.
**/ }
